    "status": "Open",
    "issue_id": "0005",
    "platform": "Intel Birch Stream SP",
    "reporter": "元始天尊",
    "rootcause": "The SetupReentryHook is called after PostManagerHandshake(), before entering Setup. \nIt is also called when returning to Setup after a Boot Override operation.\nThis hook is primarily used to handle the Setup re-entry flow and can be utilized to disable NVRAM write protection (such as the NVLock mechanism).\nThe bundled AMISetupNVLock module version is 13 or above, which has already fixed the issue of being unable to save setup settings after executing exit from the internal Shell to enter the BIOS Setup menu.",
