    "title": "Overriding the root port's PCIe device settings by project.sdl will cause a build error.",
    "status": "Closed",
    "issue_id": "0006",
    "platform": "Intel Birch Stream SP",
    "reporter": "元始天尊",
    "rootcause": "Previously, it was possible to directly override the root port's PCIDEVICE settings in project.sdl.\nHowever, in recent AptioV versions (especially on newer platforms or with the latest BIOS build tools), the structural checks for the PCI hierarchy have become stricter.\n** Copy the PCIe device that needs to be overridden to project.sdl, set disable=Yes, and then re-declare the same settings in the same project.sdl. This should allow the build to pass and resolve the failure.",
